<h1>Patricia O&#39;Brien Sheahan</h1>
<p>Judge up for retention, on the Chicago ballot November 3, 2026. Incumbent.</p>
<p>Circuit Court of Cook County</p>
<h2>Ratings</h2>
<ul>
<li>Chicago Bar Association: <a href="https://www.chicagobar.org/votejudges#:~:text=Patricia%20O%27Brien%20Sheahan" rel="nofollow noopener">Qualified</a></li>
<li>Illinois State Bar Association: <a href="https://www.isba.org/judicial-elections/counties/cook#:~:text=Patricia%20O%E2%80%99Brien%20Sheahan" rel="nofollow noopener">Yes</a></li>
</ul>
<h2>Record</h2>
<p>Elected to the Circuit Court in 2014; assigned to the Law Division, hearing civil trials including personal injury, medical malpractice, and products liability cases. Injustice Watch reports that her father-in-law is Michael F. Sheahan, the former Cook County sheriff and 19th Ward alderman. A judge stays on the bench with a yes from 60 percent of voters.</p>
<h2>Background</h2>
<p>Associate general counsel of the Shirley Ryan AbilityLab, then the Rehabilitation Institute of Chicago (1999-2014); earlier a civil litigation attorney at Baker McKenzie (1996-1999). Law degree from IIT Chicago-Kent (1996).</p>
